.claude/settings.json:795:  "_model_pin_comment": "PLAN-163 T1.1 contingency (ADR-181 §Contingency) — session-default pin. CC 2.1.220 honors the top-level settings key \"model\" (zod: E.string().optional(); describe \"Override the default model used by Claude Code\"; source at 2.1.220 binary offset 226819212, sha256 8addc857..., positioned between \"permissions\" and \"fallbackModel\" in the settings schema — NOT the internal workflow prop \"defaultModel\", NOT the env var ANTHROPIC_MODEL). Pinned to claude-opus-5-5 since ADR-149 Amendment 3 (S357; Claude Opus 5.5 needs Claude Code >= 2.1.280); from ADR-181 until then the pin was claude-opus-5 (OQ1=b primary/fallback), which stays the fallbackModel. Rationale: APPENDING claude-sonnet-5 to availableModels makes the 2.1.220 tier-default (sonnet-5) an ALLOWED model, so enforceAvailableModels no longer redirects the session away from it and the session default would silently FLIP from claude-opus-4-8 (=availableModels[0], the prior fallback target) to sonnet-5; the explicit pin forecloses that flip. The pinned value MUST remain an EXACT member of availableModels below (claude-opus-5-5 is present): SessionDefaultPinTest in .claude/hooks/tests/test_template_dogfood_parity.py compares exact ids, while Claude Code itself admits an id that extends an allowed entry by a - segment and replaces a pin the allowlist does not admit with the default model at startup (with a warning). Env ANTHROPIC_MODEL / CLI --model still override per-session at runtime. Mirror this key in templates/settings/settings.base.json or SessionDefaultPinTest reddens.",
.claude/settings.json:814:  "_deny_baseline_comment": "PLAN-153 Wave E item 3 — coarse harness-level deny baseline (docs/deny-baseline.md). Entries 5-24 of permissions.deny below mirror scripts/install.sh DENY_BASELINE_ENTRIES exactly: credential-store reads (~/.ssh, ~/.aws, npm/gcloud/kube/docker/git-credentials/netrc/pypirc), dotenv-family reads (SPECIFIC .env variants only — a deny rule cannot carry allow exceptions, so .env.example/.sample/.template stay readable by omission; unlisted variants like .env.secret pass this backstop), and the curl|bash tripwire. Honest limits: Read deny does not cover arbitrary subprocesses opening files, Bash(curl * | bash) is bypassable by rephrasing (that class is owned by check_bash_safety.py), and **/.env is cwd-anchored. Gate floor: check_harness_config.py DENY_BASELINE (4 entries — PLAN-161 C1 removed the three Write() twins: on current CLIs (>=2.1.216) Edit(X) deny rules cover ALL file-editing tools and Write(X) rules are unconsulted; the Owner accepted the old-CLI residual) must remain a subset of this list.",
.claude/settings.json:817:  "_night_mode_deny_surface_comment": "PLAN-165 P1-corrected (D2 + round-2 findings NM-01/NM-03 + codex CX-1, Owner-ratified OQ1-redo 2026-08-03) — under defaultMode=acceptEdits a tool Edit/Write is auto-accepted, so every file that can DECIDE the next session's posture is deny-listed: (1) .claude/settings.local.json — the per-machine posture overlay (gitignored); a tool write of it is the direct escalation ladder. (2) .claude/state/night-mode.json — the night-mode marker/snapshot: night-mode off restores marker.prev_value into the overlay, so a marker write is a posture write BY PROXY (NM-01). (3) .claude/scripts/night-mode.py — the single sanctioned writer (NM-03). HONEST SCOPE (CX-1): these per-TOOL deny entries close only the Edit/Write rail — deny cannot see Bash. The load-bearing rail for Bash is _CANONICAL_GUARDS in check_canonical_edit.py (all three paths added there in the SAME ceremony; check_bash_safety keys off that list), plus kernel-tier listing of the two STATE files in check_arbitration_kernel.py. night-mode.py writes the overlay and the marker as a PROCESS (tempfile + os.replace), never via tools, so none of this costs a legitimate path — and per the Owner-ratified OQ1-redo, model-rail invocation of the toggle is itself blocked: on/off are HUMAN actions (terminal or the `!` prefix). The Write() twins were REMOVED in S292: the current harness (>=2.1.216) does NOT consult Write(path) rules in its file-permission check (the CLI emits an active warning for such rules) and the Edit(path) entries cover ALL file-editing tools — the same class PLAN-161 C1 removed from the credential-read baseline; the old-CLI residual documented there is now accepted for the posture files too, with the real defense on the _CANONICAL_GUARDS/kernel rails above (CX-1). Appended AFTER the curl|bash tripwire so entries 5-24 keep mirroring install.sh DENY_BASELINE_ENTRIES by position (see _deny_baseline_comment); these three entries are NOT part of that mirror. The three entries are byte-identical in templates/settings/settings.base.json (dogfood parity).",
.claude/settings.json:833:      "Read(~/.pypirc)",
.claude/settings.json:847:      "Edit(.claude/scripts/night-mode.py)"
.claude/settings.json:866:  "_skill_budget_comment": "PLAN-135 W1 S7: skillListingBudgetFraction caps the skill-listing context tax (fraction of context window in chars; CLI default 0.01 = 8000 chars at a 200k window); skillOverrides name-only demotes 0-dispatch domain-tier skills. Regenerate: python3 .claude/scripts/skill-budget-generator.py --jq-fragment",
.claude/settings.json:972:    "command": "python3 \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/scripts/statusline-ceo.py\"",
