templates/settings/settings.base.json:2:  "_comment": "CEO Orchestration — BASE hooks (universal, stack-agnostic). Always installed. Stack-specific hooks like tsc+vitest live in settings.stack.<name>.json and are merged in by install.sh via --stack flag. The check-agent-spawn hook is CORE to the protocol — do not remove. Session 75 Codex Finding 2 parity-up with dogfood .claude/settings.json — this template ships ALL active governance hooks the framework runs (currently ~16+: canonical-edit, skill-patch, scratchpad-scope, budget, confidence-gate, output-safety, arbitration-kernel, plan-edit Edit|Write|MultiEdit, tier-policy, read-injection, MCP-response, webfetch-injection, subagent-fabrication, skill-reference-read, skill-bootstrap-post, fluency-nudge). Parity is enforced by .claude/hooks/tests/test_template_dogfood_parity.py. An adopter who wants minimal posture can hand-edit post-install — but the parity test will then warn on update.",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:13:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_agent_spawn.py",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:15:            "statusMessage": "Checking agent spawn governance..."
templates/settings/settings.base.json:20:        "_comment": "Bash safety: shlex-based parser replaces 5 substring-matching rules that false-positived on quoted strings during Sprint 2. Blocks: rm -rf (all flag combos), git reset --hard, git push --force/-f. Allows: --force-with-lease, quoted strings, compound commands with safe clauses. See check_bash_safety.py docstring for full logic.",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:25:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_bash_safety.py",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:37:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_adversary.py",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:49:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_plan_edit.py",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:56:        "_comment": "Arbitration kernel HARD-DENY (Session 75 Codex Finding 2 mirror from dogfood + PLAN-065 Layer A 2026-05-04): blocks Edit/Write/MultiEdit AND any mcp__* tool with write-shaped params against arbitration-kernel files (governance hooks, _lib primitives, policies, native subagent .md frontmatter) WITHOUT sentinel escape — only CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE+ACK env vars in the parent shell allow. Layer A closes S81-tris gap.",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:61:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_arbitration_kernel.py",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:73:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_tier_policy.py",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:85:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_read_injection.py",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:92:        "_comment": "PLAN-152 governance-03 (mirror of dogfood ADR-106 + ADR-110): PreToolUse Pair-Rail Multi-LLM hook. When Edit|Write|MultiEdit targets an L3+ canonical-guarded path, invokes Codex MCP in read-only review mode and validates the response contains no write-shaped patches. Adopters get the codex .mcp.json from install.sh, so the rail is meaningful out of the box; on Codex unavailable it fail-OPENs with a breadcrumb (adopters without Codex pay only the no-op). Kill-switches: CEO_PAIR_RAIL_DISABLE=1, CEO_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_S (default 180s; registration cap 210s — ADR-110-AMEND-2 recalibration, invariant guarded by test_pair_rail_timeout_invariant.py).",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:97:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_pair_rail.py",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:104:        "_comment": "PLAN-152 governance-03 (mirror of dogfood): Codex MCP file-write gate — blocks write-shaped Codex responses (apply_patch envelope, unified diff, JSON Patch) on the codex tool pair. Raw python3 invocation mirrors the dogfood registration form.",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:109:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_codex_filewrite.py",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:115:        "_comment": "Canonical-edit sentinel (Sprint 5 Phase 7 ADR-010 + PLAN-065 Layer A 2026-05-04): blocks Edit/Write/MultiEdit AND any mcp__* tool with write-shaped params (path/file_path/target_path/file/filename/dest/destination/target/uri) against canonical governance paths (team.md, frontend-team.md, pitfalls-catalog.yaml, skills/**/SKILL.md, domains/*/team-personas.md, domains/*/pitfalls.yaml, plus PLAN-019 expansion: all hooks, policies, SPEC, ADRs, CI workflows, CODEOWNERS, install scripts) unless a matching Owner-signed sentinel file exists. Out-of-scope paths pass through silently. Layer A closes S81-tris gap (custom MCP tools previously bypassed).",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:120:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_canonical_edit.py",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:127:        "_comment": "PROTOCOL.md semver cascade (PLAN-110 Wave D shipped v1.39.0 / wired v1.39.6 via PLAN-112-FOLLOWUP-plan-110-close S153 — closes false-closure F-1.1-1.1-7c108548 caught by S152 PLAN-112 audit). Fail-OPEN advisory: detects PROTOCOL.md edit without paired ADR-NNN-AMEND-M in same-session session_edits → emits protocol_edit_missing_amend_paired audit event + additionalContext WARN, never blocks. In-hook path filter targets PROTOCOL.md (matcher is broad per check_plan_edit.py convention). Position-in-chain: AFTER canonical-edit (sentinel-block fires first) + BEFORE skill-patch-sentinel (orthogonal scope). Doctrine port: spec-kit constitution.md:L302-L305 semver discipline.",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:132:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_protocol_semver_cascade.py",
