templates/settings/settings.stack.sandbox.json:4:  "_doctrine_comment": "Doctrine 1 (native-under-rail, never native-instead-of-rail): this fragment is a FLOOR under the hooks, not a replacement. NO hook is retired by enabling it (H4 retirement-mapping is DEFERRED — see PLAN-135 disposition ledger). check_bash_safety.py + the canonical guards keep catching INTENT; the sandbox catches MECHANICS (process containment, network egress, FS scope).",
templates/settings/settings.stack.sandbox.json:6:  "_compat_comment": "Compatibility pass over the 48 on-disk hooks (PLAN-135 W2 / staged/w2/SANDBOX-COMPAT-NOTES.md): the ONLY hooks that need NETWORK egress under the sandbox are the Codex pair-rail (check_pair_rail.py + codex_review_user_code.py -> `codex` CLI). Their endpoints are exactly the PLAN-133 sanctioned-egress SoT (_lib/egress_taxonomy.py _PAIR_RAIL_HOST_SUFFIXES) and are mirrored into allowedDomains below. NO hook invokes gpg/gh/git-push (those are Owner-ceremony shell commands run OUTSIDE the hook rail); under this fragment the Owner ceremony runs in the un-sandboxed operator shell, not inside a sandboxed Bash tool-call. Exec-only hooks (node --check, eslint, python3 -m pytest, scratch `git init/commit`) need process exec inside the sandbox but NO network.",
templates/settings/settings.stack.sandbox.json:8:  "_network_allowlist_comment": "allowedDomains = the PLAN-133 egress list. SoT = _lib/egress_taxonomy.py _PAIR_RAIL_HOST_SUFFIXES (openai.com, githubcopilot.com, codex.dev) for the Codex pair-rail, PLUS the two operationally-required hosts the compat pass surfaced (api.anthropic.com for the model API the harness itself reaches; github.com + objects.githubusercontent.com for `gh`/git operations the Owner runs and for codex's GitHub-backed auth). Extend ONLY by extending the egress SoT first, then regenerating this list — do not hand-edit divergent. deniedDomains is empty by design: the model is default-deny (allowlist wins); deniedDomains exists for adopters who widen allowedDomains and want to carve back a known-bad host.",
templates/settings/settings.stack.sandbox.json:18:      "_comment": "Paths the sandboxed Bash process may read/write. repo = the project tree (so Edit/Write/build/test all work); /tmp = scratch (mktemp scratch dirs used by review_loop.py git-init, eval/probe scratch runs, hermetic venvs). HOME is NOT writable: keeps a sandboxed command from rewriting ~/.bashrc / ~/.claude profile/credential files (harvest D5 startup-file class). $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR expands to the repo root at install time.",
templates/settings/settings.stack.sandbox.json:49:        "files.pythonhosted.org",
