.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:7:- **P1 annex — Symbolic revision names can satisfy final-review coverage.** [.claude/scripts/approval_gate.py:183](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.FGmdD8/wt/.claude/scripts/approval_gate.py:183), with validation at [line 124](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.FGmdD8/wt/.claude/scripts/approval_gate.py:124). With the supplied default policy, setting both `final_rev` and `review.reviewed_rev` to `"HEAD"` produces **rc 0, APPROVED, empty reasons**; `"unknown"` also passes. If HEAD moves after review, the unchanged symbolic strings still satisfy the comparison without identifying the reviewed commit. The declared checkpoint revision defect concerns another CLI. **Minimal fix:** require full immutable commit IDs captured when the evidence is produced; reject symbolic or malformed identifiers before comparing them.
