   417	- **Workflow orchestration, with `ultracode`.** Agents that a Workflow script
   418	  starts do not pass through the spawn gate
   419	  (`.claude/hooks/check_agent_spawn.py`), with or without `ultracode`: a
   420	  Claude Code limit recorded in the framework repository (`CLAUDE.md`, probe
   421	  `wf_d7af49d9`, PLAN-178) and seen again on 2.1.280 in probe E6, where a
   422	  PreToolUse hook matching every tool recorded no Agent event for the three
   423	  `agent()` starts of a workflow while the main session's own Agent call did
   424	  fire one. The workflow agents' own tool calls do fire PreToolUse (measured
   425	  for Bash in E6–E8), so the framework's PreToolUse guards on those tools
   426	  still see them. `ultracode` turns on dynamic workflow orchestration (the
   427	  harness's own description) and, in Auto mode, skips the first-launch
   428	  Workflow consent prompt; the agents those workflows start are agents the
   429	  spawn gate does not see.
   430	
   431	It does not change:
   432	
   433	- **The VETO floor check, though not the model of every VETO spawn.** The
   434	  spawn gate (`.claude/hooks/check_agent_spawn.py`) checks the VETO-role
   435	  agent files' own `model:` frontmatter against `VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED`
   436	  (`.claude/hooks/_lib/agent_frontmatter.py`, exact membership). It does not
   437	  read the session model, so the override neither trips that check nor
   438	  satisfies it. It does not read the model Claude passes for the invocation
   439	  either, although the PreToolUse input of an Agent call carries it as
   440	  `tool_input.model` (docs, hooks reference), and it does not see the model
   441	  Claude Code finally serves. The check vouches for the frontmatter only,
   442	  and the frontmatter decides a VETO agent's model only when resolution
   443	  reaches it and admits it. Anything that settles the model before the
   444	  frontmatter is consulted, or that rejects the frontmatter's id once it
   445	  is, runs a VETO agent on another model while the check still passes.
   446	  Those mechanisms belong to Claude Code and change between its releases:
   447	  the *Create custom subagents* docs page, sections "Choose a model" and
   448	  "Run every subagent on one model" (read 2026-09-23), describes them for
   449	  the current release. The three below are examples from that reading, not
   450	  a complete list:
   451	
   452	  - **A per-invocation model.** It outranks the frontmatter (the
   453	    resolution order above). An alias that resolves outside
   454	    `VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED` (`sonnet` or `haiku`, for example) runs the VETO
   455	    agent off the floor with or without this override. `opus` resolves to
   456	    the main session's exact model when that model is an Opus: without the
   457	    override that is the shipped pin `claude-opus-5`, which the floor lists;
   458	    under the override it is the new model, and `claude-opus-5-5`, this
   459	    page's example, is not in `VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED` as of v1.4.1-rc.1. When
   460	    the main session's model is not an Opus, `opus` resolves to the version
   461	    the alias points to, which on the Anthropic API is Opus 5.5 from Claude
   462	    Code 2.1.280 unless `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL` is set (docs, model
   463	    configuration): outside the floor as well.
   464	  - **A variable that comes before the frontmatter or replaces it.** On
   465	    Claude Code older than 2.1.196 the shipped
   466	    `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL=inherit` forced every subagent onto the main
   467	    session's model, so there the override changes the model every VETO
   468	    agent is served; from 2.1.196 `inherit` counts as unset. Before 2.1.251
   469	    a model set in `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL` came first in the order and
   470	    overrode the frontmatter. On 2.1.257 or later (that variable's floor),
   471	    while `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL_FORCE` is on, Claude Code ignores the
   472	    `model` field of every definition. No shipped template sets that
   473	    variable; leave it unset, or the VETO floor model is lost.
   474	  - **An allowlist that blocks the frontmatter's id.** Claude Code checks
   475	    the frontmatter value against the `availableModels` list in effect. For
   476	    a blocked full id it runs the subagent on the inherited model instead,
   477	    trying `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL` first when that names a model; under
   478	    this override the inherited model is the new model. At every GA tag
   479	    from v1.0.0 through v1.4.1-rc.1 the VETO-role files (`VETO_FLOOR_ROLES`
   480	    in the same module) pin `claude-fable-5`, and the maintainer
   481	    template's list admits that id. Lists from user, project and local
   482	    settings are concatenated, so in a maintainer install a list you add
   483	    there cannot remove it. A list in a managed policy replaces all the
   484	    others (docs, model configuration, "Merge behavior"), so under either
   485	    profile it blocks the id unless it admits it. A `user` profile install
   486	    ships no list, so there any list in effect blocks the id unless it
   487	    admits `claude-fable-5`: one in your user or local settings, for
   488	    example, the new-family entry
   489	    [above](#why-availablemodels-usually-needs-no-change) included. Check
   490	    with `grep '^model:' .claude/agents/*.md` which ids your definitions
   491	    pin, and keep each one in any list you add.
   492	- **The prices.** `python3 .claude/scripts/ceo-cost.py` (no slash command
   493	  ships for it) has printed two blocks by default (`--source both`) since
   494	  v1.4.0. The transcripts block (primary,
   495	  `.claude/scripts/ceo-cost-transcripts.py`) reads the model recorded on each
   496	  transcript turn, so the new id does appear there, but until a release adds
   497	  its price row it is named in a warning and priced at $0, never guessed; its
   498	  prices come from `.claude/scripts/cost-table.yaml`, or from a table
   499	  embedded in that script when the file does not parse. The
   500	  audit block (secondary) prices each spawn by the model id
   501	  `.claude/hooks/audit_log.py` records for it. In the PLAN-044 audit the
   502	  spawn's tool response carried no model on 199 of 199 spawns (an older
   503	  Claude Code; not re-measured on 2.1.280), so that id is the ADR-052 policy
   504	  id for the agent's role (for `general-purpose`, `claude-opus-5` from
   505	  v1.2.0 through v1.4.1-rc.1 and `claude-opus-4-8` from v1.0.0 through
   506	  v1.1.0), or nothing, which the audit block reports as `unknown_model` at
