   508	  the audit block's price table rather than extending it: a custom file must
   509	  carry every row you want priced.
   510	- **Your teammates.** The file is per machine and must stay out of git.
   511	  Since v1.3.0, `scripts/install.sh` and `scripts/upgrade.sh` put
   512	  `/settings.local.json` in `.claude/.gitignore` under **every** install
   513	  profile (creating the file, or appending the entry when it is missing).
   514	  They also add `.claude/settings.local.json` to the repository's root
   515	  `.gitignore` unless the profile is `user`. `install.sh` defaults to
   516	  `maintainer`, so it writes the root entry unless run with
   517	  `--ceremony user`. `upgrade.sh` takes the profile from the recorded
   518	  `.claude/.install-state.json` first, then `--ceremony`, then the
   519	  `CEO_UPGRADE_CEREMONY` environment variable; with none of these it treats
   520	  the install as `user` and skips the root file. On an older
   521	  install, or if you edited those ignore files, check with
   522	  `git check-ignore .claude/settings.local.json`: if it prints nothing, add
   523	  the path to `.gitignore` yourself before committing anything.
   524	
   525	When the framework release that adopts the model arrives, upgrade as usual
   526	([UPGRADE-PROCEDURE.md](UPGRADE-PROCEDURE.md)). If the release pins the same model, you can
   527	remove the keys from the local file; if it pins another one, the local file
   528	keeps winning on your machine until you remove them.

